# Angular Enquiry Management System - Cursor Rules

## Project Context
This is an Angular 19 application for enquiry management with:
- OAuth2/OIDC authentication via Keycloak
- Spring Boot REST API integration
- Quarkus BAMOE process management
- Material Design UI components
- Case management workflow

## Code Style & Standards

### Angular Best Practices
- Use standalone components (Angular 19+)
- Implement reactive programming with RxJS
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Follow Angular style guide conventions
- Use OnPush change detection where appropriate

### Component Structure
```typescript
// Preferred component structure
@Component({
  selector: 'app-feature',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [CommonModule, /* specific Material modules */],
  template: `<!-- template -->`,
  styles: [`/* component styles */`]
})
export class FeatureComponent implements OnInit, OnDestroy {
  // Properties
  // Constructor with dependency injection
  // Lifecycle hooks
  // Public methods
  // Private methods
}
```

### Service Patterns
- Use `providedIn: 'root'` for singleton services
- Implement proper error handling with RxJS operators
- Use environment configuration instead of hardcoded values
- Follow the service pattern: `FeatureService` for business logic

### Authentication & Security
- Always use `AuthService` for authentication operations
- Implement proper route guards with `authGuard`
