- Follow reactive patterns throughout

### Environment Configuration
- Use `ConfigService` for configuration access
- Never hardcode URLs or configuration values
- Use environment-specific configurations
- Implement feature flags for conditional functionality

### Constants & Types
- Use `APP_CONSTANTS` for application constants
- Define proper TypeScript interfaces
- Use enums for status and type definitions
- Implement type safety throughout

### Error Handling
- Use `MatSnackBar` for user notifications
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Log errors appropriately
- Provide meaningful error messages

### Testing Considerations
- Write unit tests for services and components
- Use Angular Testing Utilities
- Mock external dependencies
- Test user interactions and API calls

