## Common Patterns

### Subscription Management
```typescript
private destroy$ = new Subject<void>();

ngOnInit() {
  this.service.getData()
    .pipe(takeUntil(this.destroy$))
    .subscribe(data => {
      // Handle data
    });
}

ngOnDestroy() {
  this.destroy$.next();
  this.destroy$.complete();
}
```

### Error Handling
```typescript
this.service.getData().subscribe({
  next: (data) => {
    // Handle success
  },
  error: (error) => {
    console.error('Error:', error);
    this.snackBar.open('Error loading data', 'Close', { duration: 3000 });
  }
});
```

### Environment Usage
```typescript
// Use ConfigService instead of direct environment access
const apiUrl = this.configService.getApiUrl('enquiryService');
const isDebugMode = this.configService.isFeatureEnabled('debugMode');
```

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid
- Don't hardcode URLs or configuration values
- Don't forget to unsubscribe from observables
- Don't use `any` type unless absolutely necessary
- Don't mix business logic in components
- Don't ignore TypeScript errors
- Don't use deprecated Angular features
- Don't forget to handle loading and error states
- Don't use inline styles for complex styling
- Don't ignore accessibility requirements
- Don't commit sensitive configuration data